bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    seed_jit_dict_f64_literal_value_read_loses_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27, 0, "Repro (aarch64 JIT, base e2479b4127a0a3a9 and the typed f64? reader fix; interpreter 0.1): val d: {text: f64} = {"k": 0.1}; print d["k"] prints 0.09999999999999998, and val g: f64? = d.get("k") then g ?? 9.0 / if val / unwrap / match all read 0.09999999999999998. MIR stores the literal through rt_dict_set with the raw f64 value and reads it with rt_index_get / rt_dict_get + UnboxFloat, so the raw bits are decoded as a tagged float. Found while probing Option producers for seed_jit_explicit_f64_option_some_typed_readers_lose_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27; not an Option representation defect."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    seed_jit_dict_f64_literal_value_read_loses_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27, P3, closed, "stale: FIXED by p3sweep4-20261127 (dict literal + .set/.insert float values boxed via BoxFloat); cargo tests RED 0/4 to GREEN 4/4; sspec 3/3; 81 dict lib tests green 2026-11-27", src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/mir/lower/lowering_expr_collection.rs, 0, NONE, 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, true

bug_fix_claims |bug_id, state, session_id, claimed_at, heartbeat_at, prev_status, note|
    seed_jit_dict_f64_literal_value_read_loses_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27, fixing, p3sweep4-20261127, 2026-11-27T19:36:19Z, 2026-11-27T19:36:19Z, open, "wave9"

    seed_jit_dict_f64_literal_value_read_loses_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4-61127: reproduced with bit oracles (Python/struct): correct 0.1 = 0x3fb999999999999a, observed readback 0x3fb9999999999998 - low 3 mantissa bits zeroed; every reader (d[k], d.get(k) + ??, if val, .unwrap(), match) corrupted; fixture bitmask run mismatch 2102437. Root cause: rt_dict_set takes TAGGED RuntimeValues but lower_dict_expr boxed only integers (box_int_operand - its own comment ended Float/bool VALUE boxing remains a follow-up); every typed dict read emits UnboxFloat -> rt_value_as_float which sees the raw f64 bits (low3 = TAG_FLOAT) as a legacy inline float and decodes payload()<<3 i.e. (bits>>3)<<3 (runtime/src/value/core.rs:392-402); the .insert/.set arm had the identical raw write (d[k] = v already boxed). Fix: lowering_expr_collection.rs:597 lower_dict_expr F32/F64 via MirInst::BoxFloat (lossless rt_value_float heap box, same pattern as array/tuple literals); lowering_expr_method.rs:733 .set/.insert arm boxes floats with the same guard shape. Verification: cargo test -p simple-compiler --test seed_jit_dict_f64_literal_value_read RED 0/4 (codes 32767/65535) to GREEN 4/4; release + debug scratch builds clean; all read paths print 0.1, readers mismatch 0, bits mismatch 0 (jit + interpret); sspec test/01_unit/language/dict_f64_literal_value_exact_payload_spec.spl 3/3 with SIMPLE_BINARY=fixed (RED evidenced by the cargo test + direct fixture runs - the pre-fix seed cannot compile the current test runner); sibling seed_jit_f64_option_exact_payload 8/8; --lib -- dict 81/81. Residuals (out of scope, recorded): {text: bool} literal values still stored raw (word 1 for true aliases TAG_HEAP; round-trips int readers by accident - the comment now says so); f32? .get readers return the f64-promoted value (0.10000000149011612 on JIT vs 0.1 interpreter) - a separate inline-f64 Option-reader divergence identical before/after (the f32 spec arm pins only the dict index read). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/language/dict_f64_literal_value_exact_payload_spec.spl prevention=src/compiler_rust/compiler/tests/seed_jit_dict_f64_literal_value_read.rs"
    seed_jit_dict_f64_literal_value_read_loses_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4: reproduced with bit oracles (0.1 read back as 0x3fb9999999999998, low 3 mantissa bits zeroed; every reader corrupted; bitmask fixture mismatch 2102437). Root cause: rt_dict_set takes TAGGED RuntimeValues but lower_dict_expr boxed only integers (its own comment ended Float/bool boxing remains a follow-up); typed dict reads emit UnboxFloat -> rt_value_as_float which decodes raw f64 bits as a legacy inline float (bits>>3)<<3 (runtime core.rs:392-402); .set/.insert had the identical raw write. Fix: mir/lower/lowering_expr_collection.rs:597 F32/F64 via BoxFloat; lowering_expr_method.rs:733 same guard shape. cargo test --test seed_jit_dict_f64_literal_value_read RED 0/4 to GREEN 4/4; all read paths exact on jit + interpret; sspec dict_f64_literal_value_exact_payload 3/3; sibling f64_option_exact_payload 8/8; --lib dict 81/81. Residuals: {text: bool} literal values still raw (documented); f32? .get readers return f64-promoted values (separate inline-f64 Option-reader divergence, unchanged). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/language/dict_f64_literal_value_exact_payload_spec.spl prevention=src/compiler_rust/compiler/tests/seed_jit_dict_f64_literal_value_read.rs"
